[h1]Life Framework (Core)[/h1]

Life Framework is an open-source roleplay framework for Arma Reforger. This item is the core: the systems, the script and the neutral defaults. It has no map of its own and no setting. A pack supplies those. It is unfinished, and parts change between versions.

[h2]Looking to play?[/h2]
Subscribe to [b]Life Framework: Everon 1989[/b], the flagship pack. It is a village on Everon in 1989 and it pulls this item in, so you need nothing else.

[h2]What the core does[/h2]
[list]
[*]Jobs with levels, and money as cash, a bank account and shops.
[*]Vehicles: car lot, garage, impound, keys and locks.
[*]Crime: robberies, heists, a fence, contraband.
[*]Police: duty, ranks, dispatch, a wanted board, fines and jail.
[*]Medical: a downed state, medics and a hospital.
[*]Organizations and a shared stash.
[*]Persistence: progress is saved and carries over a server restart.
[/list]

[h2]For server owners and pack authors[/h2]
The core decides what the game can do. A pack decides what a server is: its world, place names, prices, wages, vehicles and look. A pack is data and prefabs; it holds no script.
[list]
[*]Mod ID [b]4550A2B656E1B569[/b].
[*]Requires only the base game.
[*]How the split works: [url=https://github.com/Life-Framework/Life-Framework/blob/main/docs/architecture/core-vs-pack.md]docs/architecture/core-vs-pack.md[/url]
[*]Hosting a server: [url=https://github.com/Life-Framework/Life-Framework/blob/main/docs/playtest/workshop-host.md]docs/playtest/workshop-host.md[/url]
[/list]

